{
  "title": "Colour emoji: skin tones, sequences and flags",
  "metadata": {
    "author": "pdfnative-cli samples",
    "subject": "COLRv1 colour glyphs drawn as vector forms: Fitzpatrick skin tones, ZWJ sequences, flags, and the glyphs of the 1.8.0 alpha-ramp fix (pdfnative 1.8.0)",
    "keywords": "emoji, colour emoji, COLRv1, skin tone, ZWJ, flags"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Colour emoji sequences",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Rendered with --font color-emoji --font latin --lang color-emoji,latin. Every colour glyph is a PDF Form XObject built from the font's COLRv1 layer graph — solid, linear, radial and sweep paints — with no bitmap anywhere. pdfnative 1.8.0 added COLRv1 transforms, variable paints and masks, and bundles 20 gestures and 10 generic people in all five Fitzpatrick tones: each toned form is ONE colour glyph, never a base emoji followed by a swatch."
    },
